WEBVTT

00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:22,260
Dr. Cutters, I emailed you pictures of what I believed to be a piece of the tumor that I coughed out. I'm wondering if it's possible to cough or pass tumors as a response to alternative treatments.

00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:35,260
The answer is yes, it's very possible to cough out tissue or pass tissue in the case of colon cancer or rectal cancer.

00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:52,260
It is cancerous. This has happened multiple times in the past. I've even had patients bring it in to get tested, but that's the only way you would absolutely know for sure is to bring it in a path lab and have a test in whether there's cancer cells in that.

00:00:52,260 --> 00:01:10,260
Do we know? Does it matter? Well, yes, no, you're trying to get rid of the cancer that said you're lungs. If you cough something out and there's distinct blog that looks very different. I've never had this happen before. Could this be tumor?

00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:30,260
The only way to know for sure is to get a pathology report on that, whether your path lab would do that, whether you're oncologist would play a part of that or not. I don't know, but that would be the only way to know for sure.

00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:44,260
So that's not always doable, but is it possible? That's the question. The answer is yes, it's very possible. So hopefully that is what happened.

